WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.300
Plan a trip.

2
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.140
To France? «en France».

3
00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:04.920
To Canada? «au Canada».

4
00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.280
Same English word, to.

5
00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.210
Two different French words.

6
00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:12.100
Now try Morocco, or Spain.

7
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:13.540
Which word would you pick?

8
00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:15.160
And how would you know?

9
00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:16.710
And here's another twist.

10
00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:20.320
English says in Paris, but to Paris.

11
00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:22.770
French uses one word for both.

12
00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:26.380
So why is it «en France» but «au Canada»,

13
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:30.510
and why does one French
word mean both in and to?

14
00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:34.290
In this mission, you'll follow
two figures into a town pin.

15
00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:37.450
Then you'll switch places
and directions in the lab,

16
00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:39.610
and predict each little word.

17
00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:43.470
Your mission: work out which
little word each place needs.
